  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $\u20165u-4v\u2016=26$ and $\u2016u\u2016=2$, find the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20165u-4v\u2016 & \\le \u20165u\u2016+\u2016-4v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20165u-4v\u2016 & \\le 5\u2016u\u2016+4\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 26 & \\le 5\\cdot 2+4\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 26 & \\le 10+4\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 16 & \\le 4\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 4 & \\le \u2016v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016$ is $4.$",
